  "text": "An angel shows up in a nowhere town and hands a young woman the most terrifying yes in history.\n\nGabriel gets sent to Nazareth. Not Jerusalem. Not the temple. A village.\n\nTo a virgin promised to a man named Joseph. And her name is Mary.\n\nQuick note, because everybody gets this wrong. Luke gives us the town, the fiancé, his royal line. He never gives us her age. So when you hear teenager, that's tradition talking, not the text.\n\nThe angel opens with, \"Hail, thou that art highly favoured, the Lord is with thee.\"\n\nAnd she's troubled. Not by the angel. By the greeting. She's turning the words over trying to work out what kind of hello that is.\n\nThen the news lands. You'll conceive, you'll have a son, call him Jesus, and his kingdom will have no end.\n\nNow sit in that. She's engaged. Not married. In her village, in her century, this news is not a blessing, it's a scandal that could cost her everything.\n\nAnd her one question is not can God do this. It's, \"How shall this be, seeing I know not a man?\" She's not asking for proof. She's asking how.\n\nAnd when he answers, she says, \"Behold the handmaid of the Lord. Be it unto me according to thy word.\"\n\nYes to a plan she cannot verify. In a town that could count.",
